Title:
Jailbreaker: LLM Jailbreak Testing You Can Actually Repeat

Type:
Blog Post (with accompanying GitHub Tool)

Short Summary (4-8 sentences max):
This post introduces “Jailbreaker,” a defensive LLM jailbreak testing platform aimed at making prompt-injection and jailbreak evaluations repeatable and auditable instead of ad hoc. It addresses the operational pain of manual testing (prompt sprawl, inconsistent configs, missing baselines, scattered evidence) by providing a workflow-centric UI and data model for targets, techniques, runs, and experiments. The tool includes a technique registry spanning direct/indirect prompt injection, roleplay/instruction override, obfuscation (encoding/multilingual), system prompt extraction, context poisoning, and iterative attack methods (PAIR, TAP, Crescendo, AutoDAN, GPTFuzz). It formalizes separate model roles (Target/Attacker/Judge) and supports baseline-vs-technique comparisons, dataset-by-technique experiment matrices, and results review with heatmaps/metrics plus SQL-backed analysis views. It’s useful for AI security testers, red teamers, and defenders validating mitigations over time across models and system prompts. The key value is lifecycle management: consistent execution, evidence retention, and comparability across repeated assessments.

Technical Focus:
- LLM jailbreak and prompt-injection evaluation workflows
- Technique registry (direct/indirect injection, roleplay, obfuscation, extraction)
- Iterative jailbreak automation (PAIR, TAP, Crescendo, AutoDAN, GPTFuzz)
- Baseline vs technique comparison and experiment matrices
- Multi-model role separation (Target / Attacker / Judge) and automated judging
- Results storage, heatmaps/metrics, and SQL-backed analysis/reporting

Use Cases:
- Repeatable jailbreak regression testing before/after prompt/guardrail changes
- Comparing multiple LLMs (local vs cloud) against the same unsafe-intent datasets
- Running technique-family sweeps (e.g., roleplay, injection, obfuscation) with evidence capture
- Building an internal catalog of custom techniques and scoring logic for consistent reuse
- Producing structured artifacts (CSV/JSON exports, traces, per-run evidence) for reviews and sign-off

Keywords:
LLM security, jailbreak testing, prompt injection, indirect prompt injection, system prompt extraction, roleplay jailbreak, instruction override, context poisoning, obfuscation, base64 encoding, multilingual prompts, PAIR, TAP, Crescendo, AutoDAN, GPTFuzz, attacker model, judge model, baseline comparison, experiment matrix, PostgreSQL, Docker Compose, SpecterOps Jailbreaker-CE